00000000                             9  *  #     #  #####  #     #  ####  #    #        #####   #####  #    # v2.1
00000000                            10  *
00000000                            11  *******************************************************************************
00000000                            12  * This is my own simple monitor program for my RCBus 68000 board. It supports
00000000                            13  * simple S-Record loading as well as memory display & simple memory editing.
00000000                            14  * In addition it allows reading and writing bytes to the RCBus IO space.
00000000                            15  *
00000000                            16  * There's no breakpoints, single stepping or disassembly stuff.
00000000                            17  *******************************************************************************
00000000                            18  * Hardware assumptions:
00000000                            19  *
00000000                            20  * + RC208 ROM/RAM board is used (implements ROM remapping after boot)
00000000                            21  * + My RCBus SIO board is used and an MC68681 (or equivalent) SIO chip is
00000000                            22  *   present at the address DUART1 (see devices.inc)
00000000                            23  * + ROM is present at address 0x700000 (see memory3.inc)
00000000                            24  * + RAM is present at address 0x000000 (see memory3.inc)
00000000                            25  *******************************************************************************
00000000                            26  * EEPROM programming:
00000000                            27  *
00000000                            28  * Use EASyBIN to split the S-Record into ODD and EVEN bytes.
00000000                            29  * + The *_0.BIN file goes in the U ROM socket - holding D08..D15
00000000                            30  * + The *_1.BIN file goes in the L ROM socket - holding D00..D07
00000000                            31  *******************************************************************************
00000000                            32  * Exception Handling:
00000000                            33  *
00000000                            34  * The exception vector table is copied from ROM into RAM at startup and from
00000000                            35  * then on, normal 68000 exception vector processing occurs.
00000000                            36  * Initially the vector table entries all point back to handlers in ROM but can
00000000                            37  * be overwritten to point to a user supplied handler in RAM. 
00000000                            38  *
00000000                            39  * Some Easy68k TRAP #15 text I/O routines are implemented as follows:
00000000                            40  * Currently only tasks 0,1,5,6,13 & 14 are supported.
00000000                            41  *******************************************************************************
00000000                            42  * EhBASIC Support:
00000000                            43  *
00000000                            44  * The EhBASIC s-record file can be programmed into the EEPROMs at the same
00000000                            45  * time as this monitor and should reside at address EHBASIC_BASE (see memory.inc).
00000000                            46  *******************************************************************************
00000000                            47  * Interrupts:
00000000                            48  *
00000000                            49  * An interrupt handler is setup to handle autovector level 2 interrupts from
00000000                            50  * the DUART. Make sure that the jumper is set on the SIO board for level 2
00000000                            51  * interrupts.
00000000                            52  *******************************************************************************
00000000                            53  * CP/M-68K Support
00000000                            54  * V1.3 of CP/M-68K is supported. The CPM400 s-record file should be
00000000                            55  * programmed into the EEPROMs at the same time as this monitor. CP/M will
00000000                            56  * reside at address 0x0400 onwards.
00000000                            57  *
00000000                            58  * The hardware specific BIOS should also be programmed into the EEPROMs. The
00000000                            59  * BIOS must reside at address 0x6000 onwards. 
00000000                            60  *******************************************************************************
00000000                            61  * Change Log:
00000000                            62  * 2.1 - Private monitor variables now referenced as an offset from A6
00000000                            63  * 2.0 - Updated to support RC208 auto switching memory board
00000000                            64  * 1.5 - Reinstated CP/M-68K boot!
00000000                            65  * 1.4 - Interrupt driven serial Rx added - CP/M-68K boot removed
00000000                            66  * 1.3 - Added 'B' command to boot EhBASIC from EEPROM/FLASH
00000000                            67  * 1.2 - Added 'C' command to boot CP/M-68K from EEPROM/FLASH
00000000                            68  * 1.1 - Added some EASY68K TRAP #15 functions
00000000                            69  * 1.0 - Initial release
00000000                            70  *******************************************************************************
